  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "If $f(x)=(\u23081-2x\u2309+1)^{2},$ then $f(0.2)=${{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $\u2308x\u2309$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\u2308x\u2309=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n-1<x\\le n,\\,n\\in Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=0.2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.2) & =(\u23081-2(0.2)\u2309+1)^{2} \\\\  & =(\u23081-0.4\u2309+1)^{2} \\\\  & =(\u23080.6\u2309+1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\u23080.6\u2309=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.2) & =(\u23080.6\u2309+1)^{2} \\\\  & =(1+1)^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
